th, must stay cheap): reads raw key events, resolves each one to a character using the live keyboard layout and modifier state, and appends it — along with focus-change events — to a durable, append-only log.</text></paragraph></listItem><listItem id='.14348' h='4785bcbe'><paragraph id='.14349' h='71239b47'><text id='.14350'><bold>Ingest</bold></text><text id='.14356'> (cold path): tails that log, groups events into writing sessions, and reconstructs each session's text once it closes, writing the result into a queryable, full-text-indexed store.</text></paragraph></listItem><listItem id='.14537' h='3f0c9d20'><paragraph id='.14538' h='18f3338e'><text id='.14539'><bold>Query</bold></text><text id='.14544'>: reads that store — </text><text id='.14565'><code>search</code></text><text id='.14571'> for full-text lookups across sessions, </text><text id='.14611'><code>text</code></text><text id='.14615'> for the raw captured stream over a time window — concurrently with </text><text id='.14683'><code>run</code></text><text id='.14686'>, always seeing a consistent state.</text></paragraph></listItem></list><paragraph id='.14721' h='a84287bf'><text id='.14722'>Reconstruction uses a tiered strategy depending on the app:</text></paragraph><list id='.14781' h='c7a974f5' kind='bullet'><listItem id='.14782' h='34bdaaf5'><paragraph id='.14783' h='e223188e'><text id='.14784'><bold>Tier 0 — generic buffer replay</bold></text><text id='.14814'> (always available): the decoded character stream is replayed through a virtual cursor/selection text buffer (backspace, delete, arrows, Ctrl+A, paste-from-clipboard-log). Covers any app adequately, including the terminal and Chrome in this build.</text></paragraph></listItem><listItem id='.15061' h='558ad7a0'><paragraph id='.15062' h='88639909'><text id='.15063'><bold>Tier 1 — static per-app rules</bold></text><text id='.15092'>: documented formatting conventions layered on top of tier 0, where it's cheap to add.</text></paragraph></listItem><listItem id='.15178' h='871e0a34'><paragraph id='.15179' h='03c25d25'><text id='.15180'><bold>Tier 2 — real-app replay</bold></text><text id='.15204'>: for VS Code only in this build, replay the actual captured keystrokes into a sandboxed, invisible instance of the real editor and read back its own output.</text></paragraph></listItem></list><paragraph id='.15361' h='e46181c8'><text id='.15362'>Every session gets a usable reconstruction regardless of tier — tier 2 is additive precision for VS Code, never a dependency for anything else to work.</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.23875' rev='12' h='1218dc50' heading='2'><text id='.23876'>CLI reference</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.23889' h='96df66ae'><text id='.23890'>Both commands take </text><text id='.23909'><code>--data-dir &lt;dir&gt;</code></text><text id='.23925'> (default </text><text id='.23935'><code>./brain-data</code></text><text id='.23947'>) and exit non-zero with a message on stderr on error.</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.24001' h='2510b72f' heading='3'><text id='.24002'><code>brain run</code></text></paragraph><codeBlock id='.24011' h='2191d862' language='bash'><text id='.24012'><![CDATA[brain run [--data-dir ]]>&lt;<![CDATA[dir>]]]></text></codeBlock><paragraph id='.24040' h='99db8933'><text id='.24041'>Runs until stopped (Ctrl+C or killed). Captures continuously; no other flags.</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.24118' h='634e42a7' heading='3'><text id='.24119'><code>brain query search</code></text></paragraph><codeBlock id='.24137' h='b080e38a' language='bash'><text id='.24138'><![CDATA[brain query search "]]>&lt;<![CDATA[query>" [--app A] [--from T] [--to T] [--limit N] [--data-dir ]]>&lt;<![CDATA[dir>]]]></text></codeBlock><paragraph id='.24227' h='8cd702bb'><text id='.24228'>One or more words, case-insensitive, ANDed together — every word must appear in the same session's reconstructed text. Prints JSON:</text></paragraph><codeBlock id='.24359' h='5ba2b822' language='json'><text id='.2436